  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Tuesday) \nIssued at 1126 AM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nSome light showers are expected to linger into the day on Thursday, \nespecially for the Cumberland Plateau, but the biggest impact from \nthis system (and of this forecast package) is going to be the cold \nair that will follow the passage of the cold front. Our first \nwidespread freeze of the season is on tap for Saturday morning. Most \nshould be in the mid to upper 20s, but our normally cooler spots may \nbe closer to 20 and the rest of the weekend will remain cool, as \nwell. By Monday, a slow warmup will get under way, but additional \nrainfall is nowhere to be seen for quite a while.",
